# The hub folder holds the program and your own notes in one place.
# This file is the ONE rule that says which is which: what git ignores is
# yours and travels by your private brain sync; what git tracks is the
# program and travels by git.
#
# DENY BY DEFAULT. Everything at the top level is ignored, and the program's
# own names are named back in, one line each. A new note of yours anywhere in
# this folder is yours without anyone remembering to list it.
#
# It is installed as .gitignore. Keep it tracked and unmodified: the sync tool
# checks that before it trusts the partition, and stops the hub's sync in one
# plain sentence when it cannot.

/*

!/.gitattributes
!/.github/
!/.gitignore
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/DESCRIPTION.txt
!/LICENSE
!/NOTICE
!/README.md
!/SECURITY.md
!/VERSION
!/docs/
!/evidence.py
!/fonts/
!/grok/
!/icon.png
!/laws/
!/licenses/
!/openai/
!/orchestrator.py
!/semantic-rules.json
!/skin_v2.py
!/skin_v2_fonts.css
!/sync/
!/templates/
!/tests/
!/tools/

# Caches every machine makes for itself, inside the program's folders too.
# These come after the whitelist on purpose, so they win over it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
